# 19. PROJECT PROFITABILITY ENGINE

Build automatic project profitability calculations.

Gross Margin = Revenue – Direct Project Costs.

Contribution Margin = Gross Margin – Variable Project Expenses.

Net Project Profit = Contribution Margin – Allocated Overheads.

Net Margin % = Net Project Profit / Revenue × 100.

Example:

Client revenue: ₹1,50,000.

Vendor cost: ₹96,000.

Other project expenses: ₹4,000.

Gross margin: ₹54,000.

Net project profit: ₹50,000.

Create profitability at:
- Project level.
- Location level.
- Vendor level.
- Auditor level.
- Client level.
- Monthly level.
- Financial year level.

Keep estimated and actual profitability separate.

Only approved mandays, verified costs and eligible billable values should enter final calculations.

